ROLE
You are a senior Laravel engineer on the existing Wechecha Construction ERP. Work only on the Expense Hub (finance/expense-hub) row action dropdown titled "Expense Tax & Receipt". Reuse existing code: ExpenseHubController, ExpenseHubQueryService, syncVatDecisionToLedger(), scanReceipt(), the OCR side-by-side review modal (#ocrSideBySideReviewModal), the pre-export check, and the tables expense_hub_vat_decisions, receipts, receipt_items. Do not duplicate logic. First inspect the current dropdown in index.blade.php and list which items are already wired and which are dead (no click handler, no route, or errors). Then fix only what is missing or broken.

PROBLEM
The dropdown items below are displayed, but clicking them does not do the right thing. Make every item fully functional, as specified.

GENERAL RULES FOR ALL ACTIONS
- Each action opens from the clicked row and works on that row's source_type + source_id.
- Use a modal or side drawer. Do not reload the full page. After saving, refresh only that row and the summary cards, and show a success toast.
- All saves go through ExpenseHubController::saveDecision() and then syncVatDecisionToLedger() inside a DB::transaction(). Saving twice must not create duplicate receipts or ledger rows.
- Show server-side validation errors inline next to the field.
- Respect permissions: Finance Officer can use all actions. Rows in a settled month are read-only (view only) unless the user is Finance Head.
- Log every change in an audit log (user, time, old value, new value).
- Show a loading state on buttons, and disable them while saving.
- Remove any empty or placeholder menu item (there is a blank bullet between "Verified Without Receipt" and "View Purpose & Line Items").
- Show a small status badge on the row after an action (Unverified, VAT, Non-VAT, No receipt, Withholding applied, Receipt attached).

ACTION 1: Add Receipt  ("Upload slip or scan with AI OCR")
- Opens a modal with: drag-and-drop file upload, a "Choose file" button, and a "Take photo" button on mobile (use capture="environment"). Accept JPG, PNG, PDF, max 10 MB. Show a preview thumbnail and a progress bar.
- On upload: store the file, link it to the row (receipt_path), then run AI OCR (queue the job and show a "Scanning..." state).
- OCR must return JSON: vat_category (G/S), seller_tin, seller_name, purchase_date (also convert to Ethiopian date), mrc_number, fs_number, description, unit_of_measure, quantity, unit_price, subtotal, vat_amount, total, and line items, plus a confidence score per field. Save raw_ocr_payload and ocr_confidence_score.
- When OCR finishes, open the Side-by-Side OCR Review (Action 6) pre-filled with the results.
- Fallback: if OCR fails or times out, keep the uploaded file and open the same review screen with empty editable fields. The user can fill them in manually. Never block.
- Allow replace or remove receipt before the decision is confirmed.
- Reject exact duplicates (same seller TIN + FS number + MRC) with a clear message that links to the existing record.

ACTION 2: Add VAT Payment  ("Input VAT at 15% rate")
- Opens a form with: seller TIN (10 digits, required), seller name, FS number, MRC number, receipt date, description, VAT-inclusive / VAT-exclusive toggle, amount.
- Auto-calculate base, 15% VAT, and total live as the user types. Show a warning if the VAT is not 15% of the base (small rounding tolerance).
- Include an "Attach receipt" button that triggers Action 1, and pre-fill the form from OCR if a receipt is already attached.
- Save sets vat_status = 'vat_applies', stores base_amount, vat_amount, total_amount, custom_seller_tin, custom_fs_no, custom_mrc_no, then syncs to the ledger and receipts tables. This row feeds Report A (15-column Purchase VAT Return) and the VAT pool.
- Do not allow saving as VAT without TIN, FS number, and MRC. Show which one is missing.

ACTION 3: Non-VAT Payment  ("0% VAT / TAS exempt purchase")
- Opens a form with: receipt or voucher number, receipt date, seller TIN (if available), required reason dropdown (exempt supply, non-VAT supplier, other), optional receipt attachment.
- Save sets vat_status = 'no_vat', vat_amount = 0. This row feeds Report B (9-column TAS Declaration) and never enters the input VAT pool.

ACTION 4: Verified Without Receipt  ("Petty cash / informal vendor / no slip")
- Opens a short form with: required reason (petty cash, informal vendor, lost slip, other), required free-text note, optional payee name.
- Save sets is_verified_without_receipt = true. The row counts as verified but is excluded from the VAT pool, from Report A, and from Report B. It appears only in the Master Audit Export (Report D) with a non-blocking warning.
- Show a warning that no tax credit can be claimed for this expense.

ACTION 5: View Purpose & Line Items
- Opens a read-only drawer showing: purpose or description from the source module, project or site, payee, payment method, paid by, source reference number, and the line items (description, quantity, unit, unit price, amount).
- If a receipt exists, show its OCR line items next to the source line items. Highlight mismatches.
- Show the decision history (who verified, when, and what changed).
- Include a "Download receipt" link when a file exists.

ACTION 6: Side-by-Side OCR Review
- Opens the existing review modal with the original receipt (image or PDF viewer with zoom and rotate) on the left and editable extracted fields on the right.
- Fields below 70% confidence get an amber highlight. Show warnings for: invalid TIN, buyer TIN not 0038480010, VAT not equal to 15% of base, base + VAT not equal to total, duplicate receipt, and a mismatch with the cash amount paid.
- Buttons: "Confirm and save as VAT" (goes to Action 2 logic), "Confirm and save as Non-VAT" (Action 3 logic), "Re-scan", and "Cancel". Nothing is saved until the user confirms.
- If no receipt is attached, show an "Upload receipt" prompt that goes to Action 1.

ACTION 7: Full Studio (3% WHT, TAS)
- Opens one combined screen that lets the user set everything for this row in one place: VAT status (VAT 15% / Non-VAT / No receipt), receipt upload and OCR, and the 3% withholding toggle.
- When withholding is on: withholding_amount = 3% of the pre-tax base, net payable = gross minus withholding, plus an upload field and serial number field for the WHT voucher slip. A missing slip is allowed, but the row shows a "Missing slip" alert in the Withholding Slips tab.
- Allow withholding to be combined with VAT or Non-VAT outcomes.
- Show a live summary: base, VAT, withholding, net paid, and which reports and ledger tabs this row will appear in.

TESTING (feature tests)
- Each of the 7 actions opens and saves correctly through its route, and invalid input returns validation errors.
- Add VAT row appears in Report A only. Non-VAT row appears in Report B only. Verified Without Receipt appears in Report D only.
- Withholding row appears in the Withholding tab and Slips tab.
- Duplicate receipt is blocked, and saving the same decision twice does not create duplicate rows.
- Settled-month rows cannot be edited by a Finance Officer.
- OCR failure still lets the user finish manually.

DELIVERABLES
1. A short audit of the dropdown: which items worked, which were dead, and why.
2. The fixes (routes, controller methods, Blade, JS, services), keeping changes minimal.
3. Tests.
4. A final checklist, one line per action, saying how I can test it manually in the browser.

If something blocks you, ask me one question. Otherwise state your assumption and continue.